  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Clean Cooking Solutions in Southern Africa and Indian Ocean Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">remains fragmented and underfunded. The dominating use of low-efficiency biomass cooking solutions comes with major negative environment, socio-economic, health and gender impacts. Significant additional financing and policy efforts in the region are required to reach universal access to clean cooking by 2030.Well aligned with the international and regional clean cooking commitments, the  Action intends to contribute to increasing and accelerating the access to affordable, clean and sustainable cooking solutions in Southern Africa and Indian Ocean Region. It will foster clean cooking business development with coaching, financial partnership brokering (finance catalyst) and innovative financial solutions for small and medium enterprises (SMEs), including manufacturers, distributors and importers of clean cooking solutions, and training of finance institutions. More particularly, it will offer results-based-finance and thematic grants to support and accelerate market development and innovation, and it will train and provide sector-specific tools to financial institutions to expand their portfolio of financial products to SMEs of the clean cooking sector and consumers. Furthermore, the Action will strengthen the regulatory and market framework by supporting regional dialogue and coordination of policies and plans through platforms, networks of taskforces, and by promoting the elaboration of regional performance standards and their implementation guidelines, contributing to stronger clean cooking strategies and facilitated international trade of clean cooking solutions. This Action will contribute to the regional priority area 3 of the MIP &#xbf;Green Transition&#xbf; and to its specific objective 2 &#xbf;Support the development of an efficient, sustainable and resilient African energy sector&#xbf;.. The action will also actively contribute to the pledge of the Clean Cooking Declaration of Paris (2024) to make clean cooking a priority and enhance the efforts toward achieving universal access for all.The action will contribute to affordable and clean energy access for cooking (SDG7), climate mitigation (SDG13), forest conservation (SDG15), gender equality, including in enterpreneurship (SDG5), health, more particularly of women and girls (SDG3), and sustainable cities (SDG11).</narrative>
  </description>
